1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,400
Section 2

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:04,972
Hi everyone, welcome to the Snow Centre.

3
00:00:04,972 --> 00:00:05,733
My name's Annie.

4
00:00:05,733 --> 00:00:11,367
I hope you enjoyed the bus trip from the airport - we've certainly got

5
00:00:11,367 --> 00:00:13,100
plenty of snow today!

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,904
Well, you've come to New Zealand's premier snow and ski centre,

7
00:00:16,904 --> 00:00:21,400
and we've a whole load of activities for you during your week here.

8
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:26,832
Most visitors come here for the cross-country skiing, where you're on fairly flat ground

9
00:00:26,832 --> 00:00:31,100
for most of the time, rather than going down steep mountainsides.

10
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,425
There are marked trails,

11
00:00:32,425 --> 00:00:36,400
but you can also leave these and go off on your own

12
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,050
and that's an experience not to be missed.

13
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:44,124
You can go at your own speed - it's great aerobic exercise if you

14
00:00:44,124 --> 00:00:45,295
really push yourself,

15
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:49,198
or if you prefer you can just glide gently along

16
00:00:49,198 --> 00:00:51,150
and enjoy the beautiful scenery.

17
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:55,150
This afternoon, you'll be going on a dog-sled trip.

18
00:00:55,150 --> 00:01:00,377
You may have seen our dogs on TV recently racing in the winter sled

19
00:01:00,377 --> 00:01:00,750
festival.

20
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:04,710
If you want, you can have your own team for the afternoon

21
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:09,000
and learn how to drive them, following behind our leader on the trail.

22
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,600
Or if you'd prefer, you can just sit back in the sled

23
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,700
and enjoy the ride as a passenger.

24
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:17,766
At the weekend, we have the team relay event,

25
00:01:17,766 --> 00:01:20,150
and you're all welcome to join in.

26
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:22,497
We have a local school coming along,

27
00:01:22,497 --> 00:01:25,850
and a lot of the teachers are taking part too.

28
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:29,050
Participation rather than winning is the main focus,

29
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:32,650
and there's a medal for everyone who takes part.

30
00:01:32,650 --> 00:01:35,694
Participants are in teams of two to four,

31
00:01:35,694 --> 00:01:39,500
and each team must complete four laps of the course.

32
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:43,933
For your final expedition, you'll head off to Mount Frenner wearing a pair of

33
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:48,050
special snow shoes which allow you to walk on top of the snow.

34
00:01:48,050 --> 00:01:52,817
This is an area where miners once searched for gold, though there are very

35
00:01:52,817 --> 00:01:55,200
few traces of their work left now.

36
00:01:55,200 --> 00:02:00,010
When the snow melts in summer, the mountain slopes are carpeted in flowers

37
00:02:00,010 --> 00:02:00,750
and plants.

38
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:03,533
It's a long ascent, though not too steep,

39
00:02:03,533 --> 00:02:08,054
and walkers generally take a couple of days to get to the summit

40
00:02:08,054 --> 00:02:08,750
and return.

41
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:12,600
You'll spend the night in our hut half-way up the mountain.

42
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,900
That's included in your package for the stay.

43
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:20,400
It's got cooking facilities, firewood and water for drinking.

44
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:26,050
For washing, we recommend you use melted snow, though, to conserve supplies.

45
00:02:26,050 --> 00:02:30,703
We can take your luggage up on our snowmobile for you for just ten

46
00:02:30,703 --> 00:02:31,700
dollars a person.

47
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:35,960
The hut has cooking facilities so you can make a hot meal in the evening

48
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:36,528
and morning,

49
00:02:36,528 --> 00:02:38,800
but you need to take your own food.

50
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:42,650
The weather on Mount Frenner can be very stormy.

51
00:02:42,650 --> 00:02:47,600
In that case, stay in the hut - generally the storms don't last long.

52
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:52,309
Don't stress about getting back here to the centre in time to catch the

53
00:02:52,309 --> 00:02:55,000
airport bus - they'll probably not be running anyway.

54
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,440
We do have an emergency locator beacon in the hut

55
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:02,912
but only use that if it's a real emergency, like if someone's ill

56
00:03:02,912 --> 00:03:03,600
or injured.

57
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:08,967
Now, let me tell you something about the different ski trails you can follow

58
00:03:08,967 --> 00:03:10,500
during your stay here.

59
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:14,900
Highland Trail's directly accessible from where we are now.

60
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:20,928
This trail's been designed to give first-timers an experience they'll enjoy regardless of their age

61
00:03:20,928 --> 00:03:21,731
or skill,

62
00:03:21,731 --> 00:03:25,750
but it's also ideal for experts to practise their technique.

63
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:27,443
Then there's Pine Trail ...

64
00:03:27,443 --> 00:03:32,100
if you're nervous about skiing, leave this one to the experts!

65
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:37,200
You follow a steep valley looking right down on the river below - scary!

66
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:42,050
But if you've fully mastered the techniques needed for hills, it's great fun.

67
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:47,050
Stony Trail's a good choice once you've got a general idea of the basics.

68
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:49,945
There are one or two tricky sections,

69
00:03:49,945 --> 00:03:51,600
but nothing too challenging.

70
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:55,976
There's a shelter half-way where you can sit and take a break

71
00:03:55,976 --> 00:03:57,800
and enjoy the afternoon sunshine.

72
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:00,900
And finally, Loser's Trail.

73
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:06,186
This starts off following a gentle river valley but the last part is quite exposed

74
00:04:06,186 --> 00:04:09,710
so the snow conditions can be challenging - if it's snowing

75
00:04:09,710 --> 00:04:14,643
or windy, check with us before you set out to make sure the trail's

76
00:04:14,643 --> 00:04:15,700
open that day.

77
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:16,092
Right,

78
00:04:16,092 --> 00:04:20,400
so now if you'd like to follow me, we'll get started ...
